==English==

===Alternative forms===
*[[double-whammy]]

===Etymology===
The phrase is thought to have been popularized by [[cartoonist]] [[w:Al Capp|Al Capp]] (1909&ndash;1979), from his classic [[comic strip]], ''Li'l Abner''.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|head=[[double]] [[whammy]]|double whammies}}

# a [[twofold]] [[blow]] or [[setback]]; a series of two events that cause adverse effects